  (text "Cell + lead: put a 15 A blade fuse in an inline holder close to the cell (off-board)."
    (at 25 144.0 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid dcee6588-eb4b-4956-8d2a-8afda705804a))
  (text "R201: 10 mOhm 2512 shunt (Isabellenhuette CMS, 2.5 W) in the cell negative lead, so it measures BOTH charge and discharge. Pads 2/3 are Kelvin taps at the inner pad edges."
    (at 25 148.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid f60185a5-9a0b-4fb6-9df7-a2c511c4abfa))
  (text "JP201 is the single GND-PGND link (a wire link next to the shunt). Do not add another ground connection between the two nets."
    (at 25 153.0 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid f4b67c04-3b9e-4688-ac78-11d44bc380cd))
  (text "K1 (charger) and K2 (load): Panasonic ALFG2PF121, 12 V coil, 33 A, normally open. Coils run from +12V_SW, so any fault opens both."
    (at 25 157.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid 1e7ddacd-bfd0-4ebe-b14e-9f4e2c27773e))
  (text "Interlock: Q203 holds K1 off while K2_EN is high and Q204 holds K2 off while K1_EN is high (both commanded = both off)."
    (at 25 162.0 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid 3e156585-3683-4e7c-9d31-347692c4304f))
  (text "Coil drivers Q201/Q202 are BC337 (bipolar) so a 3.3 V GPIO switches them fully. R203/R206 keep the relays off while the MCU boots."
    (at 25 166.5 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid 9a86f24c-89ad-407a-8974-4c7d4bd254ec))
  (text "How it works / what to check: docs/SCHEMATIC_GUIDE.md section 2."
    (at 25 171.0 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left top))
    (uuid e2d1f163-d577-46b0-97be-16d19e8db144)))
